  "facts": [
    "The SMART Tunnel, Malaysia's longest dual‑purpose tunnel, stretches 9.7 km, with a 13.2‑m diameter stormwater tube that opened in 2007, diverting floods while still carrying traffic.",
    "When heavy rains hit, the tunnel activates Mode 4, pumping up to 5 million cubic metres of water in 22 hours, a feat that saved Kuala Lumpur from catastrophic flooding in December 2021.",
    "Built by a joint venture of Gamuda and MMC, the tunnel used two German Herrenknecht TBMs, one of which completed a 737‑m section in just 24 weeks in December 2003."
  ],
